# ── Rust ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/target
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak

# ── Vendored cargo / rustup cache used by the Dockerfile builder ──────
/.cache/

# ── Release artifacts built by the Makefile / scripts ────────────────
/dist/

# ── Node / Vite (client & client-app frontends) ──────────────────────
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
apps/lantunnel-client/frontend/dist/
**/.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Android mobile app build outputs ────────────────────────────────
apps/android-proxy/.gradle/
apps/android-proxy/.kotlin/
apps/android-proxy/app/build/
apps/android-proxy/app/src/main/jniLibs/

# ── iOS mobile app generated native libraries / Xcode user state ────
apps/ios-proxy/NativeLibs/*.xcframework/
apps/ios-proxy/NativeLibs/TpMobileFfiBuild/
# The Xcode project is generated from project.yml by `xcodegen generate`.
apps/ios-proxy/TunnelProxyIOS.xcodeproj/
apps/ios-proxy/ExportOptions-AppStore.plist
apps/ios-proxy/DerivedData-*/

# ── Python bytecode caches ───────────────────────────────────────────
**/__pycache__/

# ── Tauri generated sources & per-build overrides ────────────────────
apps/lantunnel-client/src-tauri/gen/
apps/lantunnel-client/src-tauri/.tauri-build-override-*.json

# ── Runtime logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log

# ── Local config overrides (not checked in) ──────────────────────────
*.local.yaml
*.local.yml
*.local.toml
# Per-machine Apple signing identity consumed by the Makefile.
release.local.mk
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
.env.local
.env.*.local
# Legacy release credentials may still exist on maintainer machines. Keep
# them ignored even though the active release path no longer reads this file.
upload.env

# ── Secrets / TLS material — users supply their own at runtime ──────
certs/*.key
certs/*.crt
certs/*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.p8

# ── Editor / OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Claude Code session state (kept local) ───────────────────────────
.claude/
.superpowers/
state/

# ── Local agent/operator instructions (kept local, never published) ──
# These carry Apple Developer account identity, production platform
# hostnames, business-model notes, and paths into the private platform
# repository. They are working notes for the maintainer's machine, not
# contributor documentation — see CONTRIBUTING.md for that.
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md

# ── Local TODO plans (kept on the maintainer's machine, never published) ──
/docs/plans/

# ── Local build summary scratch files ────────────────────────────────
client-summary.txt
gw-summary.txt

# ── Local E2E evidence ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Run artifacts, not source.
tests/e2e/_fixtures/.matrix-out/

# ── Phase 2 latency JSON metric reports ──────────────────────────────
# `tp-e2e-p2 --test <name>` writes `latency_<name>_<cell>.json` to the
# CWD when invoked directly by a V2 harness.
# These are run artifacts, not source.
/latency_*.json

# ── Phase 3 throughput JSON metric reports ───────────────────────────
# `tp-e2e-p3 --test <name>` writes `throughput_<name>_<cell>.json` to
# the CWD. Same rationale as the latency artifacts above.
/throughput_*.json

# ── Performance benchmark output ─────────────────────────────────────
# Historical run reports are no longer tracked. Benchmark scripts still
# write here on a maintainer machine; keep the whole tree local.
reports/

# The shared UI bundle is staged into each phone by `make _stage-android-ui`
# and `make _stage-ios-ui`. It is build output of apps/lantunnel-client/frontend,
# not source; committing it would let a phone ship screens older than the code.
apps/android-proxy/app/src/main/assets/ui/
apps/ios-proxy/TunnelProxy/Resources/ui/

# Android release signing. The keystore lives outside the repository; this
# file carries its passwords and must never be committed.
apps/android-proxy/keystore.properties
*.jks
*.keystore
